    18	======================================
    19	
    20	a) Concrete behavior and trace
    21	   - Base task: a black n×n mover slides through blue river pixels toward a red n×n
    22	     destination. Motion is BFS over top-left placements whose whole n×n window lies in
    23	     {river, mover, destination}.
    24	   - Original reachable behavior: mover reaches the red square and overwrites it with
    25	     black; start square turns blue.
    26	   - Original stuck behavior: mover advances to the farthest reachable placement before
    27	     the sub-n chokepoint; start turns blue.
    28	   - Combo reachable behavior (D6/3): when BFS can reach the destination placement,
    29	     both the black mover and red destination are erased to river color. The whole
    30	     corridor becomes pure blue.
    31	   - Combo stuck behavior (D13/2): when BFS cannot reach the destination, the mover does
    32	     not advance at all. Output is identical to input.
    33	   - Small trace with n=2:
